.TH HOODMIN-CLI 8 "2026-11-03" "Hoodmin 0.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hoodmin-cli \- configure, maintain and manage Hoodmin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hoodmin-cli [--config FILE] COMMAND
.SH COMMANDS
config show|set: inspect redacted settings or configure database/HTTPS from a private URL file.
.br
config web --serve-static true|false [--directory DIR]: select built-in or direct Nginx static serving.
.br
database init|check: provision local or remote PostgreSQL and apply checksummed migrations.
.br
owner-init --email ADDRESS: create the initial owner and store credentials in a root-only file.
.br
api login|get|post|logout|whoami: use the shared management API with a human session or bot token.
.br
keys status|rotate --confirmed: inspect key IDs or transactionally rewrap all encrypted fields. Keep an independent verified backup first.
.br
backup policy|prune [--apply]: configure retention or preview/apply removal of verified backups.
.br
backup create|export|pull: create, encrypt or fetch backups. pg_dump and age are optional external tools.
.br
service start|stop|restart|status|enable|disable: control the local service.
.br
acme-hook: internal Certbot HTTP01 callback.
.br
upgrade [--watch|--status|--request|--wait SECONDS]: root-only resumable upgrade coordinator. Normally managed by hoodmin-upgrade.service and package postinst. SQL uses the native Rust driver; pg_dump is required for pre-migration backups.
.br
upgrade --configure --admin-url-file FILE: save a protected remote administrator URL file targeting the same application database. Local peer administration needs no file.
.SH SECURITY
TCP PostgreSQL connections require sslmode=verify-full.
Read database URLs, passwords and bot tokens from private files instead of command arguments.
Mutating human API calls require both Origin and CSRF; role and tenant checks match the web interface.
.SH SEE ALSO
hoodmin(8), /usr/share/doc/hoodmin/docs/cli.md
